# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# 301s from the OLD strikearms.ie PHP site -> new URLs (preserve link equity).
# Activate at cutover. Targets marked (future) must exist before the old site is
# taken down, or point them at a live parent until then.
/Airsoft-and-the-Law.php    /airsoft-law              301
/Where-to-Play.php          /where-to-play            301
/Care-for-your-Rifle.php    /guides/airsoft-maintenance  301
/About-Airsoft.php          /guides/beginners-guide   301
/guns-n-gear.php            /store                    301
/Contact-us.php             /contact                  301

# /search is not a page. Search results are /store?q=, which is the same
# grid with the same filters and sorting -- a second URL for it would be a
# duplicate of a page that is already noindexed. This is here because
# people type it. Pages carries the query string over when the target has
# none of its own, so /search?q=m4 lands on /store?q=m4.
/search                     /store                    301

# No SPA fallback rule, on purpose. Pages applies _redirects BEFORE static
# files ("Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset
# matches"), so a catch-all like `/* / 200` also rewrites /assets/*.js and
# *.css to the HTML shell and the site renders blank. With no 404.html in the
# build, Pages already serves index.html for any path that is not a file,
# which is the SPA fallback we want. Do not add a /* rule back, and do not add
# a 404.html without adding the fallback another way.
